Make the check success lines name their controls

The success line of assert-shadow held the words "fails" and "broken".
The success line of assert-latch held the words "failure lines". Both
lines go to standard output, which the two scripts keep for a pass. A
reader of a build log therefore found a failure word on the channel of
the pass. That reader read a green run as a red one.

The new lines name the controls. assert-shadow rejects control copies,
which is the vocabulary of the comment above its own controls.
assert-latch calls the fault a control. Its lines of the code 5 then
read as the proof that the check finds the fault.

The live counts, the two channels, the failure lines on standard error
and every exit code stay as they were. No script and no build rule
reads the success prose of either check.

The change sits on the branch work/gtk4-theme of the local tree, as the
seventh commit. The fork wyn/qtcurve holds that branch. Merge request !15 on
system/qtcurve holds that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/gtk4/check/assert-latch.sh b/gtk4/check/assert-latch.sh
index ce0f353b..4d640c7b 100644
--- a/gtk4/check/assert-latch.sh
+++ b/gtk4/check/assert-latch.sh
@@ -98,5 +98,5 @@ if ! kill -0 "$pid" 2>/dev/null; then
     echo "assert-latch: the watch mode stopped after the fault" >&2
     exit 1
 fi
-echo "assert-latch: the fault gave $five failure lines of the code 5, and the" \
-     "pass after it gave a line of its own"
+echo "assert-latch: the count of the lines of the code 5 under the" \
+     "control fault is $five. The pass after the fault gave a line of its own"
diff --git a/gtk4/check/assert-shadow.sh b/gtk4/check/assert-shadow.sh
index dea02425..e921068a 100644
--- a/gtk4/check/assert-shadow.sh
+++ b/gtk4/check/assert-shadow.sh
@@ -168,4 +168,4 @@ sed 's/margin: 10px/margin: 11px/' "$on3" > "$tmp/byte.css"
 control byte "$tmp/byte.css" "$off3" "$on4" "$off4" "$shipped3"
 
 echo "assert-shadow: the two arms hold the contract of '$psel', and the" \
-     "check fails each of the $broken broken sheets"
+     "check rejects each of the $broken control copies"
